# Security headers for every asset/navigation response served by the static-assets
# layer (Cloudflare Workers honors this file). /api/* and /media/* are answered by
# the Worker (run_worker_first) and are not covered here — they return JSON/media,
# not documents, so the CSP that matters guards the HTML shell below.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is the seatbelt behind the render-time HTML
# sanitizer: script-src 'self' (no 'unsafe-inline') means even a sanitizer bypass
# can't run inline script. frame-src is the ONLY place third-party frames are
# allowed, and it lists exactly the video-embed origins from shared/embeds.ts —
# keep the two in sync when adding a provider.
#
# script-src also allowlists Cloudflare's own Web Analytics beacon
# (static.cloudflareinsights.com) — harmless to add (it's Cloudflare's own
# infrastructure, not third-party) and without it the beacon script is silently
# blocked, so enabling Web Analytics on the zone does nothing. Its reported data
# goes to /cdn-cgi/rum on this same origin (a Workers custom domain is proxied
# through Cloudflare), which connect-src 'self' already covers.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https: data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; media-src 'self' https:; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.twitch.tv https://clips.twitch.tv https://player.vimeo.com https://streamable.com https://docs.google.com
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
